libbacktrace, vendored for the crash report (support/d2_crash.cpp).

Upstream:  https://github.com/ianlancetaylor/libbacktrace
Commit:    0b9b49cf4a2c9229fc052d6716e1528b2f23e91a (2026-09-03)
License:   BSD-3-Clause, see LICENSE

Only the files the PE/COFF reader needs on Windows are kept:
  alloc.c dwarf.c fileline.c pecoff.c posix.c read.c sort.c state.c
  backtrace.h internal.h filenames.h LICENSE README.md
config.h and backtrace-supported.h are hand-written for i686-w64-mingw32 in
place of the autoconf output. Compiled as C (gnu99).

Local changes, all in pecoff.c and marked "Redivivus local change":
  - coff_debug_in_image(): the Windows loader maps every PE section, so the
    DWARF sections are read from the loaded image instead of being copied out
    of the file into one allocation the size of all debug info (hundreds of MB
    for d2.exe, which a 32-bit process near a crash may not have). Falls back
    to the upstream file read when a section is not mapped and readable.
  - dll_notification(): upstream assigns the callback's data pointer to
    error_callback; it now takes context->error_callback.
  - coff_add(): the COFF symbol table is rebased onto the loaded module
    address instead of the preferred image base, so syminfo names the right
    function in a relocated image.
